# LIBRARY: own
# Object.entries() that a for-of takes apart at once gives one list of keys and values in a row, and the verifier lets only the reads of that loop name it. The list bears the note that it is as made, and the rows of those reads say `relies = Pristine`: under testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime the question once named the list too, and check=Validate stopped the build of every such loop. The program never sees that list, so nothing can be done to it: it is not asked.
